## The GCAL 8X Premium

**The GCAL 8X Premium is the additional cost of choosing a GCAL-certified lab stone over an IGI-certified stone at the same grade — and what you actually get for it.** At 2ct, GCAL D-VVS1 costs $2,883 vs IGI D-VVS1 at $2,403. The difference is $480. Here is what that buys.

GCAL's 8X report grades a stone on 8 categories. These are: Light Performance, Polish, Symmetry, Fluorescence, Colour, Clarity, Cut, and Proportions. Every grade carries a guarantee — if a GCAL-certified stone fails its stated grade when independently tested, GCAL replaces or compensates. [GCAL (gcalusa.com)](https://www.gcalusa.com/) offers this on all 8X certified stones.

IGI certifies over 85% of the lab marquise inventory at this size. IGI grades are reliable at [igi.org](https://www.igi.org/) for colour and clarity. IGI does not offer the performance guarantee that GCAL's 8X standard includes.

**When the $480 GCAL premium is worth it:**
- You want the strongest possible documentation for resale at 2ct
- You're buying as a significant gift and the performance guarantee matters to the recipient
- You plan to pass the ring down and want the most defensible certificate
- You have the budget and the 8X guarantee gives you confidence you cannot get from IGI

**When to choose IGI and keep the $480:**
- You are wearing the ring, not documenting it for resale
- You understand IGI grading and trust the certificate for your own purchase
- You want to put the $480 toward a better setting

