**Verdict:** GCAL D-VVS1 at $2,883 is the right choice if the 8X grade guarantee matters to you at 2ct. IGI D-VVS1 at $2,403 is the right choice if the cert standard is sufficient and you want the $480 back. Both stones look identical on the finger. The difference is purely the document behind the stone.

## Entry Tier — IGI 2ct E-VVS1 and E-VVS2 ($2,212–$2,232)

The entry floor for true 2.00ct lab marquise in current certified inventory is $2,212 — IGI E-VVS1 Ideal.

**What you get at $2,212:** E colour — essentially colourless and visually identical to D. VVS1 clarity — inclusions are extremely difficult to find under 10x magnification. Ideal cut grade. This is the cheapest 2ct certified lab marquise with VVS clarity. Face-up: approximately 14x7mm — 15–20% more than a 2ct round.

The second entry stone is IGI E-VVS2 Excellent at $2,232. That is $20 more for VVS2 clarity — one grade below VVS1. Both are eye-clean. Both look identical on the finger. The $20 difference is not meaningful. Choose by cut grade preference (Ideal vs Excellent) and 360° video L:W ratio.

**Natural comparison at this tier:** Natural G-VS2 at 2ct costs ~$8,000. The lab E-VVS1 is a better grade at 72% less. The lab grades higher AND costs less — the 7x premium is visible even at the entry comparison.

