> **"At 2ct, I always check the 360° video before recommending any marquise — lab or natural. The bow-tie shadow is more visible at larger sizes because the stone is longer and the belly section is wider. I've rejected D-VVS1 stones that had a harsh bow-tie and selected E-VS1 stones that looked clean and brilliant. The grade on the cert matters. The light performance on the video matters more."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

## GCAL Tier — GCAL 2ct D-VVS1 ($2,883)

The GCAL D-VVS1 Ideal at $2,883 is the strongest documented 2ct lab marquise under $3,000 in certified inventory.

**What GCAL 8X adds over IGI:** GCAL grades the stone on 8 performance categories with a written guarantee. The colour grade is D. The clarity grade is VVS1. The cut grade is Ideal. Every one of those grades is guaranteed by [gcalusa.com](https://www.gcalusa.com/) — not just stated. If independently tested and the stone fails its grade, GCAL covers it.

**The $480 premium over IGI D-VVS1:** You pay $480 for the 8X guarantee. The stone looks identical to the $2,403 IGI D-VVS1. The only difference is the document.

**Who buys GCAL at 2ct:** If you are spending $3,000–$5,000 on a 2ct ring, you likely want the strongest cert available. GCAL D-VVS1 is that certificate. It is the right choice if the 8X performance guarantee matters to you — not just a grade statement.

